maluos-estate (0.9.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 14 slice 4b (docs/phase14-watching-agents.md): the collectors.
    The node's report gains three parts for the watching agents on the
    kernel server, numbers and short facts only:
    postgres (a database server, or a host whose own cluster holds its
    data): connections against the limit, the longest transaction and lock
    wait (seconds and the pid, never the query), WAL, replication, sizes,
    dead tuples and vacuum age, transaction-id age, ERROR/FATAL/PANIC
    counts in the server log since the last report, the server
    certificate's days left, superusers other than postgres. Read as the
    node service's user by peer authentication (pg_monitor only).
    linux: failed units, a pending reboot and since when, clock sync,
    inode use.
    security: failed logins and their top sources, logins from addresses
    not seen before, sudo uses and their users, what listens beyond
    loopback, a digest of /etc/maluos and of the units with the time it
    last changed, the firewall.
  * The node service's user joins systemd-journal and adm (the journal,
    the PostgreSQL server log). What the collectors remember between
    reports is /var/lib/maluos/estate/collect.json (0600).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:10:00 +0000

maluos-estate (0.8.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 14 slice 4a (docs/phase14-watching-agents.md): a bare node.
    maluctl estate join URL --code CODE --bare joins a server that has no
    vault and no gateway (a database server): no host principal, no agents,
    no inference, no memory, no overlay. The node token and the node key
    are files of the node service's user (/var/lib/maluos/estate/node.token
    and node.key, 0600, the directory 0700) instead of vault entries. The
    node heartbeats, reports and runs the actions its list allows
    (apply_updates by default). leave and status know a bare node.
  * A join without --bare on a server with no vault says so instead of
    failing in the vault's client.
  * The node's facts carry its role (database-server, application-server,
    kernel) from first boot's record; the office labels the node with it.
  * On a database server the report's units are the cluster, the engine's
    listener and the node service: the idle vault and gateway are not
    reported as down.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:20:00 +0000

